able\nL67: \nL68: Impurities:\nL69: \nL70: IgG, tested\nL71: \nL72: Technical Service\nL73: \nL74: Need help? Our team of experienced scientists is here for you.\nL75: \nL76: 【7†Let Us Assist】\nL77: \nL78: * * *\nL79: \nL80: * * *\nL81: \nL82: Properties\nL83: \nL84: ### Product Name\nL85: \nL86: Probumin^{®} Bovine Serum Albumin Universal Grade, pack of 100 g\nL87: ### biological source\nL88: \nL89: bovine serum\nL90: \nL91: ### Quality Segment\nL92: \nL93: 【8†300】\nL94: \nL95: ### assay\nL96: \nL97: ≥98% (purity)\nL98: \nL99: ### form\nL100: \nL101: lyophilized powder\nL102: \nL103: ### shelf life\nL104: \nL105: 48 mo.\nL106: \nL107: ### mol wt\nL108: \nL109: apparent mol wt 66 kDa\nL110: \nL111: ### purified by\nL112: \nL113: heat shock fractionation\nL114: \nL115: ### packaging\nL116: \nL117: pack of 100 g\nL118: \nL119: ### manufacturer/tradename\nL120: \nL121: Probumin^{®}\nL122: \nL123: ### origin\nL124: \nL125: USA origin\nL126: \nL127: ### technique(s)\nL128: \nL129: ELISA: suitable, enzyme immunoassay: suitable\nL130: \nL131: ### dilution\nL132: \nL133: (Serology)\nL134: \nL135: ### impurities\nL136: \nL137: IgG, tested\nL138: \nL139: ### loss\nL140: \nL141: ≤5%\nL142: \nL143: ### pH range\nL144: \nL145: 5.0-5.4\nL146: ### anion traces\nL147: \nL148: chloride (Cl^{-}): 0.0-3.0 mg/g\nL149: \nL150: ### cation traces\nL151: \nL152: Na: 0.0-10.0 mg/g\nL153: \nL154: ### foreign activity\nL155: \nL156: Bluetongue, none detected, Vesicular Stomatitis Virus, none detected\nL157: \nL158: ### storage temp.\nL159: \nL160: 2-8°C\nL161: \nL162: Description\nL163: ### General description\nL164: \nL165: This BSA powder is manufactured by a proprietary heat-shock fractionation process, using caprylic acid as an albumin stabilizer. A highly consistent and widely used grade of BSA powder for a wide spectrum of immunoassays, cell culture and microbial fermentation applications. This BSA is low in sodium and chloride as well as highly monomeric. Purity specification is >= 98%; typical purity is 100%.\nL166: ### Application\nL167: \nL168: Probumin^{®} BSA products are fit for use as blockers, protein/antibody (conjugate) stabilizers, and in immunoassays (EIA, RIA and serology systems).\nL169: ### Features and Benefits\nL170: \nL171:   * High-quality and reliability. Assurance of consistency in performance and supply.\nL172:   * Proprietary heat shock and cold solvent fractionation process optimizes the protein yield, purity, and efficacy of BSA. Large batch capacity.\nL173:   * Safe serum sourcing from USDA-licensed facilities exclusively from U.S. cattle.\nL174:   * Standard product.\nL175:   * Wide range of utility.\nL176: \nL177: ### Legal Information\nL178: \nL179: Probumin is a registered trademark of Merck KGaA, Darmstadt, Germany\nL180: ### Disclaimer\nL181: Probumin^{®} BSA grades are distinguished by differences in production. The use of terms such as ′Diagnostic Grade′ or ′Vaccine Grade′ in product names solely indicates that said products are commonly used by customers in those applications. We have not qualified every single product in every conceivable application. Users should qualify Probumin^{®} BSA grades using the specific reagents, conditions, and constraints of their assay.\nL182: For further manufacturing use only. Not for human or animal consumption.\nL183: * * *\nL184: \nL185: * * *\nL186: ### Still not finding the right product?\nL187: \nL188: Explore all of our products under 【9†Probumin^{®} Bovine Serum Albumin Universal Grade】\nL189: \nL190: 【9†View All Products】\nL191: \nL192: * * *\nL193: \nL194: ## Safety Information\nL195: \nL196: ### Storage Class\nL197: \nL198: 11 - Combustible Solids\nL199: \nL200: * * *\nL201: \nL202: ## Documentation\nL203: \nL204: Certificate of Analysis[Button: Certificate of Quality]\nL205: \nL206: * * *\nL207: \nL208: Choose from one of the most recent versions:\nL209: ### Certificates of Analysis (COA)\nL210: \nL211: Lot/Batch Number\nL212: \nL213: * * *\nL214: \nL215: Don't see t